{"headword":"בֹּ֫שֶׂם","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.m.</strong> <sup>1 K 10:10</sup> <strong>spice, balsam, balsamtree (</strong>Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">بَشَامٌ</span>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">בּוּסְמָא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܶܣܡܳܐ</span>, Gk. βάλσαμον; cf. Löw<sup>53</sup><strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:24\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.24\">Is 3:24</a> +, <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּ֫שֶׂם</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">Ex 30:23</a> v. infr., <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5:1</a> (as if from <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּשָׂם</span>); pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:6\" href=\"/Exodus.25.6\">Ex 25:6</a> + 18 times, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּשָׂמָיו</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">Ct 4:16</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>spice, perfume, sweet odour</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:24\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.24\">Is 3:24</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">קִנְּמָן־בֶּשֶׂם</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">Ex 30:23</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב׳</span> perhaps so pointed to distinguish it from) <span dir=\"rtl\">קְנֵה־בֹשֶׂם</span> v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 30:23\" href=\"/Exodus.30.23\">23</a>;—with this cf. Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">ܩܢܝܐ ܕܒܣܡܐ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">קני בוסמא</span>;—<em>spices</em> as costly, token of wealth <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:13\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.13\">2 K 20:13</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 39:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.39.2\">Is 39:2</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 32:27\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.32.27\">2 Ch 32:27</a>; royal gifts <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:2\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.2\">1 K 10:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.10\">10</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:25\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.25\">25</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:1\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.1\">2 Ch 9:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:19\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:24\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.24\">24</a>; cf. sg. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 10:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.10.10\">1 K 10:10</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 9:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.9.9\">2 Ch 9:9</a>; as article of commerce <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:22\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.22\">Ez 27:22</a>; burnt at burial <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:14\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.14\">2 Ch 16:14</a>; appointed for ingredient of the anointing oil <a data-ref=\"Exodus 25:6\" href=\"/Exodus.25.6\">Ex 25:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:8\" href=\"/Exodus.35.8\">35:8</a> cf. v <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:28\" href=\"/Exodus.35.28\">28</a> (all P), cf. <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:30\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.30\">1 Ch 9:30</a> (Palm. v. supr.); stored in temple <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 9:29\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.9.29\">1 Ch 9:29</a>; used for purifying the women of Ahasuerus <a data-ref=\"Esther 2:12\" href=\"/Esther.2.12\">Est 2:12</a>;"}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"elsewhere only <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:10\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.10\">Ct 4:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.14\">14</a> <em>spices</em>, v <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 4:16\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.4.16\">16</a> <em>balsam-juice</em>, gathered <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:1\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.1\">Ct 5:1</a>; <em>balsam-tree</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">הָרֵי ב׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 8:14\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.8.14\">Ct 8:14</a>; <em>beds of balsam</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲרֻגוֹת בּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 6:2\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.6.2\">Ct 6:2</a>; cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲרוּגֵת בּ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 5:13\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.5.13\">Ct 5:13</a> sim. of lover’s cheeks."}],"num":"2."}]},"rid":"BDB01514","strong_numbers":["1313","1314"],"next_hw":"בָּֽשְׂמַת","prev_hw":"בֶּ֫שֶׂם","all_cited":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["1411"],"TWOT":["290a"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}